  "notes": "Implements the fixture-first ML-Y-109 continuation over the existing composed-claim dependency-closure contract. The Explorer feature validates bounded requests and public-safe projections, maps SUPPORTED and QUALIFIED closure to cited ANSWER states, maps unresolved closure to ABSTAIN, preserves fixed DENY/ERROR copy, enforces request/claim identity and EvidenceRef subset binding, sanitizes negative Evidence Drawer state, labels AIReceipt references as process memory, and proves keyboard/focus/Escape behavior through browser fixtures. It adds no live API route, model call, source activation, policy authority, evidence resolution, release, deployment, publication, or public-use authority."
